.TH SQL 1 "2026-11-09" "sql unit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sql, sql_<command> \- typed SQL over ordinary directory trees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sql
.I command
[\fB\-\-context\fR \fIhandle\fR] [\fB\-\-cwd\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR \fIms\fR]
[\fB\-\-bind\fR \fIname type value\fR]...
.RI [ statement ]
.br
.B sql_\fIcommand\fR
[options]
.RI [ statement ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A table is a directory holding a \fI.table\fR definition; records are directories at the schema's
RECORD level and fields are the files inside them. The statement is a single shell argument.
An omitted table operand means the working directory (or \fB\-\-cwd\fR).
The complete reference, with EBNF for every clause, filesystem effects, errors and verified
examples, is \fBMANUAL.md\fR in the sql unit directory (\fB~/sql/MANUAL.md\fR).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create | define
TABLE [path] (schema) [VALIDATE ONLY] [UNMATCHED ERROR|IGNORE] [LINKS REJECT|INTERNAL];
VIEW [path] AS SELECT ... | LINKED AS SELECT ... | LINKED BRANCHES (name AS SELECT ... ; ...)
.TP
.B describe
TABLE|VIEW [path] [AS DDL]
.TP
.B show
TABLES IN p | VIEWS IN p | TRANSACTIONS ON root | CONTEXTS ON root | DEPENDENTS OF t | REFERENCES OF t
.TP
.B select
proj[, ...] [FROM p] [WHERE e] [ORDER BY e [ASC|DESC]] [LIMIT n] [OFFSET n]
[OUTPUT JSON|LINES|NUL|RAW] [REQUIRE MATCH]; BRANCH name proj ... in a branches root
.TP
.B insert
[INTO p] RECORD 'path'|GENERATED [UNDER 'g'] [USING (n,...)] (f,...) VALUES (v,...);
[INTO p] ADD TO f VALUES (v,...) WHERE e|ALL RECORDS; value: [NAMED 'n'] literal|FILE('path')
.TP
.B update
[p] SET f = v[, ...] [WHERE e] [ALL RECORDS|ALL MEMBERS]
.TP
.B delete
[FROM p] [MEMBERS f] WHERE e | ALL RECORDS | ALL MEMBERS
.TP
.B link | unlink
[FROM p] FIELD f TO 'rec/member' FROM SOURCE t WHERE e|ALL RECORDS; [FROM p] FIELD f WHERE e|ALL RECORDS
.TP
.B alter
TABLE [p] RENAME RECORD 'a' TO 'b' | ADD FIELD decl | DROP FIELD f [INCLUDING DATA] |
RENAME FIELD|CAPTURE a TO b | ALTER FIELD f SET|DROP ... | SET UNMATCHED|LINKS ... | ADOPT IDS
[VALIDATE ONLY]; VIEW [p] PRUNE GENERATIONS [KEEP n]
.TP
.B drop
TABLE|VIEW [p] [INCLUDING DATA] [RESTRICT] [VALIDATE ONLY]  (CASCADE: status 7)
.TP
.B check
TABLE [p] [ALL|SCHEMA|NAMES|COUNTS|TYPES|LINKS|JOURNALS] [DEEP] | VIEW [p]
.TP
.B begin | commit | rollback
begin [READ ONLY|READ WRITE] [ON root] [CONTEXT h]; commit [CONTEXT h] [RETURNING TRANSACTION]
.TP
.B context
CREATE [ON root] [OWNER pid] | SHOW [h] | SET [h] var = v | CLOSE [h] | CLEAN STALE ON root |
INSPECT h | RESUME h [OWNER pid] | MIGRATE h
.TP
.B recover
TABLE|DATABASE [p] ALL|TRANSACTION id [APPLY|REPORT ONLY]
.TP
.B trigger
INIT [ON t] | CREATE name [ON t] AFTER kinds [OF (f,...)] [WHERE e] EXECUTE '/abs' ARGUMENTS (...)
[TIMEOUT ms] [RETRIES n] [ENABLE|DISABLE] | SHOW [ON t] | ENABLE|DISABLE|DROP name [ON t]
.TP
.B watch
[ON t] FOR ALL|name [ONCE|CONTINUOUS] [RESUME] [DURATION ms] | VIEW p [DURATION ms] [DEBOUNCE ms]
.TP
.B tblmem | viewmem | ctxmem | trgmem
decode a map as a replayable script, or assign C.TraceLevel / C.DDL / C.Query / C.LockTimeout / ...
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SQL_CONTEXT
context handle (as \fB\-\-context\fR).
.TP
.B DATABASE_DIR
root for \fBcontext CREATE\fR without ON (no other use).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 ok, 2 syntax, 3 I/O or lock, 4 constraint, 5 REQUIRE MATCH empty,
6 committed but pending (run recover; never retry blindly), 7 unsupported form.
.SH FILES
\fI.table\fR, \fI.view\fR, \fI.sql/\fR (events, shared, ids, deps, .triggers, fanout, fanin),
\fI.context/<pid>/\fR, \fI.sql-root\fR, \fI.sql-journal.<id>/\fR, \fI.sql-id\fR, \fI.sql-null.<member>\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
MANUAL.md, TRANSACTIONS.md, VIEWS.md, MULTI_VIEWS.md
